The recordings used in Music_Part1 study consisted of 5 seconds selection from audio tracks provided by and through the courtesy of Smithsonian Folkways Recordings, from the studies by Clayton et al., (2022) on OSF Home, from Wiki-Commons, from Free Music Archive, from Pixabay, and the website of PacDV. Some recordings can be found in the articles of Durojaye et al. (2021) and Van Hedger et al. (2019).


Audio files were 5s long, cut from the provided recording with Audacity (version 3.0.2), normalized and pre-processed (fade in and fade out) with To Audio Convertor software (version 1.0.16).

Details for each audio file can be found below.


